# Keep line endings stable across the Windows engineering host, macOS CI and Linux CI.
#
# The repository stores text with LF. Without this, a checkout on Windows converted whole files to
# CRLF and 105 of them showed as modified with no substantive change, which buried the real edits.
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalizes on commit and checks out LF everywhere, including Windows.
#
# Shell scripts and the Theos/Make build files must be LF or they fail: `#!/bin/bash\r` is not a
# valid interpreter path, and make treats a trailing CR as part of a target name.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
*.mk      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.plist   text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png     binary
*.ttf     binary
*.car     binary
*.deb     binary
*.zip     binary
*.dylib   binary
